# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provenance: introduced by the v3.2.0 deploy-readiness security-only cycle
#   (canonical single source of truth for the production Vite build env-var contract).
# Tripod Closure: see `app/docs/ops-notes.md` #v3-2-0-deploy-readiness-and the
#   Adopted sibling H3 row #adopted-v3-2-0-deploy-readiness-security-only.
# Anchor Covenant (env-var keys): the canonical VITE_SUPABASE_URL + VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#   contract is consumed at `vite build` time per Vite's `.env.production` semantic load
#   order; deployers must REPLACE BOTH placeholders below with their actual Supabase
#   project's API_URL + ANON_KEY values BEFORE invoking `npm run build` against this file
#   (Vite auto-loads `.env.production` at build time when present, supplementing `.env`).
# Disambiguation: PRODUCTION-BUILD env-var template; not for development (dev uses
#   `app/.env` or runtime-injected VITE_* env vars via `scripts/run-e2e.sh`).
# Tag Chain: synced as of audit-cycle-v3.2.0 (security-only sub-cycle).
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECURITY: this file is safe to commit because all values are documented PLACEHOLDERS.
# Real production secrets live in app/.env.production (gitignored per .gitignore entry
# below) and are populated per-deployment from a secrets manager (1Password, Vault,
# Supabase Dashboard → Settings → API, etc.). NEVER commit real VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
# values — anon keys are technically public but binding them to git history forces a
# key rotation if the file is ever exfiltrated.

# Public-facing Supabase project URL (no trailing slash).
# Find at: Supabase Dashboard → Settings → API → Project URL
# Example: https://abcdefghij.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=[REDACTED: replace with your Supabase project URL]

# Public anon key (binds the SPA to your Supabase project's RLS policies).
# Find at: Supabase Dashboard → Settings → API → Project API keys → anon / public
# Example: eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6...
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=[REDACTED: replace with your Supabase project anon key]

# OPTIONAL: a base path prefix if deploying under a non-root URL
# (uncomment + set if hosting under e.g. https://example.com/omnisight/)
# VITE_BASE_PATH=/omnisight/
